# Role A — Voiceprint tool. Copy to .env.local to override defaults.

# --- Capture store (Role B handoff) ---
# Leave unset to persist leads locally to /data/leads.json (default, demoable solo).
# Set to B's capture endpoint / Supabase function URL to forward the locked row:
#   { id, email, role, handle, writing_sample, voiceprint_json, created_at }
# If B returns { rank, total } we surface it on the reveal; otherwise we show the local rank.
# LEAD_FORWARD_URL=
# LEAD_FORWARD_KEY=

# --- Voiceprint engine (Role D handoff) ---
# The mock analyzer in lib/voiceprint.ts needs no key. When D's Claude prompt is
# ready, wire it inside app/api/voiceprint/route.ts and add:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
